From: EglantinePS5 <noreply@eglantineps5.local>
Subject: [PATCH] Migrate 0303-fable-mesh-compute-0182-run-only-listed-mesh-programs-as-compute.patch

Source: 0303-fable-mesh-compute-0182-run-only-listed-mesh-programs-as-compute.patch
(EDEN_NX2_MESH_COMPUTE_ONLY)

With EDEN_NX2_MESH_AS_COMPUTE=1 every task/mesh pipeline ran as compute at once. A GPU hang
needs someone at the console, so the first runs should try one draw family at a time.

EDEN_NX2_MESH_COMPUTE_ONLY=<hash>[,<hash>...] (hex shader hashes: the task-or-lone-mesh
program, unique_hashes[1], or the mesh program, unique_hashes[3], as the "Mesh pipeline ...
runs as compute" and "first draw" lines and the EDEN_NX2_MESH_SPIRV_DUMP file names give
them) lets only pipelines with one of these programs run as compute. The others are not
built and their draws stay skipped, as without the compute switch; each is logged once:
"Mesh pipeline not in EDEN_NX2_MESH_COMPUTE_ONLY, draws skipped: task/mesh <h1>, mesh <h3>".

So EDEN_NX2_MESH_COMPUTE_ONLY=none (no hash parses) is a census run: as safe as today, no
mesh pipeline built, and the log lists every task/mesh pipeline the scene uses by its two
hashes. Pick one and list it in the next run.

Unset: no filter, as before. Without EDEN_NX2_MESH_AS_COMPUTE=1 the switch does nothing.
The check runs where the pipeline cache already refuses task/mesh pipelines on a device
without VK_EXT_mesh_shader, before any translation. Syntax-checked with clang against the
Vulkan headers; not built or run.

Moved for next18, code unchanged: the new function stands before PreloadAllPipelines, since
the end of that namespace is where 0330 adds MeshDiskCache.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
